{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Narrowed the CI watch a second time -- a known owned blocker is not an actionable alert\n\nRun 33844898387 woke me as FAILED(post-fix, ACTIONABLE); its sole failing job was scanner-integration\nagain, which belongs to another session. Left as-is, that filter would wake me for EVERY change's CI\nrun with the same non-actionable result -- five open changes cycling through CI, indefinitely.\n\nTightened: a failure is now suppressed when its ONLY failing job is scanner-integration. Anything\nelse fires as FAILED(ACTIONABLE, non-scanner). Main branch-head results still come through\nunconditionally, pass or fail, because those are the primary-job signal.\n\nSecond narrowing tonight. Same reasoning both times, and the same reasoning behind two of the tickets\nI filed (f850 windows, 337e chromium): AN ALERT THAT ALWAYS FIRES CARRIES NO INFORMATION, and worse,\nit trains the reader to skim the channel it arrives on. Hand-filtering a known result at 1am is how a\ngenuine one gets missed.\n\nAlso checked WHAT DID NOT RUN on that run, per the habit that has paid off five times tonight: the\nskipped jobs were 'documentation gates (docs-only route)' and a mutation shard -- both legitimate\nrouting, not silent omissions. Worth confirming rather than assuming, since a skip is exactly what\nthe scanner job is now doing on the branch-head lane while still failing on patchsets."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788508081110498001,"uuid":"2ecbe7b8-8fd8-4ed9-a517-831b2aed74b8"}